{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">CREATE DATASET statement</span>\n","class":"manual","created":1470,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/309156","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/CREATE-DATASET-statement.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/CREATE-DATASET-statement.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"CREATE-DATASET-statement\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">CREATE DATASET statement</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"CREATE-DATASET-statement__section_N1002D_N1002A_N10001\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Creates a ProDataSet object dynamically at\nrun time. The ProDataSet object that is created is empty. </p>\n      <div class=\"note note note_note\" id=\"CREATE-DATASET-statement__note_N10037_N1002D_N1002A_N10001\"><span class=\"note__title\">Note:</span> You can use the <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"ADD-BUFFER-method.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ADD-BUFFER-method.html\">ADD-BUFFER( ) method</a> and <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"SET-BUFFERS-method.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/SET-BUFFERS-method.html\">SET-BUFFERS( ) method</a> to add\nbuffers to a dynamic ProDataSet object. </div>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"CREATE-DATASET-statement__syntax_GC15A52683812\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d272177e112\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"CREATE-DATASET-statement__idGDG22V2664684\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>CREATE DATASET <var class=\"keyword varname\">dataset-handle</var> <strong class=\"ph b synmeta\">[</strong> IN WIDGET-POOL <var class=\"keyword varname\">widget-pool-name</var> <strong class=\"ph b synmeta\">]</strong></code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <dl class=\"dl parml\">\n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">dataset-handle</var>\n          </dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">A variable of type HANDLE that represents the handle of the dynamic\nProDataSet object.</dd>\n        \n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">IN WIDGET-POOL <var class=\"keyword varname\">widget-pool-name</var></dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">An expression of type CHARACTER that evaluates, at run time,\nto the name of the widget pool in which the dynamic ProDataSet object\nis created.<div class=\"note note note_note\" id=\"CREATE-DATASET-statement__note_N100BD_N100B9_N100AC_N10095_N1004B_N1002A_N10001\"><span class=\"note__title\">Note:</span> Widget pool names are not case-sensitive.</div></dd>\n        \n      </dl>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"CREATE-DATASET-statement__notes_GC15A62683823\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d272177e177\">Notes</h2>\n      \n      <ul class=\"ul\">\n        <li class=\"li\">If\nyou do not specify a widget pool name, the object is created in the\nSession unnamed widget pool (not in the closest unnamed widget pool).\nThe object goes away when its widget pool goes away or when you delete\nit using the <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"DELETE-OBJECT-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/DELETE-OBJECT-statement.html\">DELETE OBJECT statement</a>.</li>\n        <li class=\"li\">If the ProDataSet object serves as an OUTPUT parameter and you specify\na widget pool, the widget pool must outlive the called procedure.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"CREATE-DATASET-statement__example_GC15A72683829\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d272177e196\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">Following\nis an example of how to create a dynamic ProDataSet object for Orders\nand their Orderlines:</p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"CREATE-DATASET-statement__idGDG22X2664693\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>DEFINE VARIABLE hDset AS HANDLE NO-UNDO.\nDEFINE VARIABLE hRel  AS HANDLE NO-UNDO.\n\nCREATE DATASET hDset.\n\nhDset:SET-BUFFERS(BUFFER ttOrder:HANDLE, BUFFER ttOrderLine:HANDLE).\n\nhRel = hDset:ADD-RELATION(BUFFER ttOrder:HANDLE, BUFFER ttOrderLine:HANDLE,\n  &quot;OrderNum,OrderNum&quot;).</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"CREATE-DATASET-statement__see-also_GC15A82683833\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d272177e225\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"ProDataSet-object-handle.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ProDataSet-object-handle.html\">ProDataSet object handle</a>, <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"DEFINE-DATASET-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/DEFINE-DATASET-statement.html\">DEFINE DATASET statement</a></p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"CREATE-DATABASE-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/CREATE-DATABASE-statement.html\">CREATE DATABASE statement</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"CREATE-DATA-SOURCE-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/CREATE-DATA-SOURCE-statement.html\">CREATE DATA-SOURCE statement</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/309156","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":1318,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"CREATE DATASET statement","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/CREATE-DATASET-statement.html","type":"Manual"}